  "_note": "The generated players' profiles, by role (maintainer, 2026-11-12: random but sensible, recognisable). Each value is [mean, spread]. A characteristic is derived by key, so the same world gives the same player: value = mean + spread * z, clamped to [0.02, 0.98], with z in [-1, 1] mixing the player's own key (1 - family_weight) and a key shared by his family of characteristics (family_weight), so that what goes together goes together (an explosive player is usually fast). The body (height, weight) is derived the same way. The strong foot follows the passing profile; the weak foot is a fraction of it (weak_foot_ratio); left_footed_share of the players are left-footed. Edit a role, replay the same seed, and the players change: no code to touch.",
  "_source": "Orders of magnitude of real football: goalkeepers and centre backs are the tallest, wide players the lightest and fastest, strikers finish, centre backs tackle and head, midfielders pass and read; about a quarter of players are left-footed. Not calibrated on data: the real distributions are the generator's job (L3, IDEA-DESIGN-007), and this file is its declared prototype."
